WEBVTT

1
00:00:11.134 --> 00:00:18.857
The servants had decorated the schoolroom for Sara's birthday party.

2
00:00:18.858 --> 00:00:22.881
Miss Minchin and Sara led all the girls inside.

3
00:00:22.882 --> 00:00:27.158
Three servants, including Becky, followed the procession.

4
00:00:27.159 --> 00:00:31.503
The servants all carried boxes of presents, which they placed on a table.

5
00:00:31.504 --> 00:00:35.630
Becky had forgotten herself in the midst of the excitement of the party.

6
00:00:35.631 --> 00:00:41.860
Now she was grinning at Lottie, who was wriggling happily as she waited for Sara to open her presents.

7
00:00:41.861 --> 00:00:49.882
Miss Minchin frowned. "You may leave now," she told Becky and the other servants.

8
00:00:49.883 --> 00:00:54.499
"Please, Miss Minchin," Sara said suddenly, "may Becky stay?

9
00:00:54.500 --> 00:00:57.702
I know she'd like to see the presents."

10
00:00:57.703 --> 00:01:05.660
Miss Minchin put on her glasses and looked Sara up and down. "Becky?"

11
00:01:05.661 --> 00:01:10.936
"She's just a child too, you know," Sara added boldly.

12
00:01:10.937 --> 00:01:14.119
For a moment Miss Minchin didn't speak.

13
00:01:14.120 --> 00:01:18.418
"My dear Sara," she managed to say at last.

14
00:01:18.419 --> 00:01:23.308
"Kitchen maids are not children."

15
00:01:23.309 --> 00:01:27.869
"Well, Becky is a child," Sara repeated.

16
00:01:27.870 --> 00:01:31.222
"Please let her stay because it's my birthday."

17
00:01:31.223 --> 00:01:36.897
Becky had been backing away, nervously twisting the bottom of her apron.

18
00:01:36.898 --> 00:01:44.485
The headmistress sighed. "Very well. As a birthday favor, she may stay.

19
00:01:44.486 --> 00:01:49.209
Becky, you must thank Miss Sara for her great kindness."

20
00:01:49.210 --> 00:01:52.714
At Miss Minchin's reply, her face lit up.

21
00:01:52.715 --> 00:01:57.731
"I'm very grateful, miss!" she said, grinning at Sara.

22
00:01:57.732 --> 00:01:59.998
Miss Minchin waved her hand.

23
00:01:59.999 --> 00:02:03.305
It was in the direction of the corner near the door.

24
00:02:03.306 --> 00:02:12.934
"Stand over there, Becky," she commanded. "Away from the other girls!"

25
00:02:12.935 --> 00:02:18.761
Soon Miss Minchin left the room, and all the girls rushed toward the boxes.

26
00:02:18.762 --> 00:02:24.476
Sara opened the biggest one first. Inside was the Last Doll.

27
00:02:24.477 --> 00:02:32.123
"Oh!" groaned the children in delight. The new doll was truly magnificent.

28
00:02:32.124 --> 00:02:37.303
Lottie gasped. "She's almost as big as I am!"

29
00:02:37.304 --> 00:02:41.202
"She's dressed for the theater!" Ermengarde said.

30
00:02:41.203 --> 00:02:45.756
"Her cloak is lined with fur, and she has an opera glass."

31
00:02:45.757 --> 00:02:51.999
"Here's her trunk," said Sara. "Let's open it and look at her things."

32
00:02:52.000 --> 00:02:57.892
Sara sat on the floor and turned the key. The girls crowded around her.

33
00:02:57.893 --> 00:03:01.268
Never had the schoolroom been so noisy.

34
00:03:01.269 --> 00:03:05.228
Sara held up each item as she removed it from the trunk.

35
00:03:05.229 --> 00:03:11.695
There were dresses, ballgowns, jewelry, hats, lace collars, and fans.

36
00:03:11.696 --> 00:03:16.624
Even Lavinia and Jessie were impressed by the contents of the trunk.

37
00:03:16.625 --> 00:03:20.136
Sara put a black velvet hat on the doll.

38
00:03:20.137 --> 00:03:25.455
"Let's pretend she understands that we're admiring her," she said.

39
00:03:25.456 --> 00:03:30.947
"You're always pretending things," Lavinia said in a superior tone.

40
00:03:30.948 --> 00:03:36.245
Sara looked up. "Yes, I am," she said. "It's fun."

41
00:03:36.246 --> 00:03:40.514
"Well, it's easy to pretend if you're rich," said Lavinia.

42
00:03:40.515 --> 00:03:44.510
"Could you do it if you were a beggar and lived in an attic?"

43
00:03:44.511 --> 00:03:50.073
"I think I could, but it wouldn't be easy," Sara answered.

44
00:03:50.074 --> 00:03:53.465
Just then Miss Amelia came into the room.

45
00:03:53.466 --> 00:03:58.163
"Sara, your papa's lawyer, Mr. Barrow, has come to see Miss Minchin.

46
00:03:58.164 --> 00:04:02.448
Your birthday feast is ready in her sitting room. Lead the other girls there.

47
00:04:02.449 --> 00:04:05.746
Miss Minchin needs to meet with Mr. Barrow in here."

48
00:04:05.747 --> 00:04:10.820
Sara did as she was told.

49
00:04:10.821 --> 00:04:16.651
"Go back to your work, Becky," said Miss Amelia. Then she left the room.

50
00:04:16.652 --> 00:04:19.635
Becky stayed behind in the room for a minute.

51
00:04:19.636 --> 00:04:26.301
Miss Amelia had told her to go back to work, but Becky couldn't help taking another look at the doll.

52
00:04:26.302 --> 00:04:29.983
She picked up the doll's hat and then a coat.

53
00:04:29.984 --> 00:04:35.865
Suddenly she heard Miss Minchin coming! Becky darted under the table.

54
00:04:35.866 --> 00:04:39.503
She hoped the tablecloth was long enough to hide her.

55
00:04:39.504 --> 00:04:45.944
The headmistress came into the room, followed by a small gentleman who looked rather disturbed.

56
00:04:45.945 --> 00:04:51.178
"Please have a seat, Mr. Barrow," Miss Minchin said as she sat down.

57
00:04:51.179 --> 00:04:57.009
But Mr. Barrow was too fascinated by the large doll and her wardrobe to sit.

58
00:04:57.010 --> 00:05:00.407
"Such a fancy gift for a child!"

59
00:05:00.408 --> 00:05:04.714
"Captain Crewe is a wealthy man," said Miss Minchin.

60
00:05:04.715 --> 00:05:07.330
"His diamond mines alone—"

61
00:05:07.331 --> 00:05:10.653
"Diamonds!" Mr. Barrow interrupted.

62
00:05:10.654 --> 00:05:15.380
"There were no diamonds in those mines. Never were."

63
00:05:15.381 --> 00:05:20.220
"What?" Miss Minchin stood up. "What do you mean?"

64
00:05:20.221 --> 00:05:27.911
"It was a bad investment," Mr. Barrow went on. "The late Captain Crewe—"

65
00:05:27.912 --> 00:05:34.942
Miss Minchin gasped. "'The late Captain Crewe'? You mean he's dead?"

66
00:05:34.943 --> 00:05:40.118
"Yes, that's what I've come to tell you," explained the lawyer coldly.

67
00:05:40.119 --> 00:05:44.995
"He died from jungle fever and stress caused by his business troubles.

68
00:05:44.996 --> 00:05:50.312
An old friend invested all Captain Crewe's money in the mines and then ran away.

69
00:05:50.313 --> 00:05:54.582
Captain Crewe lost everything he owned."

70
00:05:54.583 --> 00:05:57.993
Miss Minchin dropped back into her chair.

71
00:05:57.994 --> 00:06:04.363
"Does this mean Sara is a pauper instead of a princess?" she cried.

72
00:06:04.364 --> 00:06:06.961
"Who will take care of her?"

73
00:06:06.962 --> 00:06:11.407
"You're responsible for her now," said Mr. Barrow.

74
00:06:11.408 --> 00:06:19.573
"She doesn't have a relative left in the world."
